{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_34br4cscpvapwfxbvhylo2diaev2gaqnsxctajbsf3r3rg6kvj4a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — all four phases pass.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src` is a single 37-line translation unit exporting one symbol: `void driver(int x)`, which prints the 4 object-representation bytes of `x` as lowercase hex via `printf(\"%02x\", …)` plus a newline. The internal `static void print_hex(unsigned char*, int)` is the only other function.\n\n## Phase A — surface mapped (artifacts in crate root)\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | Translation-unit inventory + `nm -D` dumps for both `.so`s. C exports `driver` only; Rust exports `driver`. **Symbol diff empty (0 missing)**. Both C functions are genuinely translated — nothing stubbed, no module skipped. All Rust undefined symbols are glibc/libgcc/weak-CRT. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 13 rows, all `[x]`. Mechanical greps proved the C has **zero** validation and **zero** error channel (no `return`, `assert`, range/null check, enum, or `#define`; `printf`'s return value ignored at both call sites). Rows therefore cover the only real error surface: the `i < len` guard (E1/E2), \"nothing is ever rejected\" (E3), silently-swallowed `printf` failures with `EBADF`/`ENOSPC`/`EPIPE`/sticky-`ferror` (E4–E7), `static` symbol unreachability (E8), plus mandated generic boundaries G1–G5 (no pointer param → documented + header-asserted; one-past-range wrapping; the enum analogue = dirty upper 32 register bits). |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 27 rows, all `[x]`. Axes derived from the source: per-byte value class (`0x00`, `<0x10`, letter nibbles, `≥0x80`), byte position 0–3, sign, embedded NULs, calls-per-stream, C/Rust interleaving, `stdout` buffering (`_IOFBF`/`_IOLBF`/`_IONBF`/pipe), calling thread, locale, and FFI marshalling. |\n\n## Phases B–D — 42 differential tests, all passing\n\nBoth `.so`s are loaded with `libloading` and driven **only** through `dlsym(\"driver\")` — the `#[no_mangle]` wrapper is under test. ~175 000 invocations per library are compared byte-for-byte, including two exhaustive 65 536-value sweeps and fixed-seed randomized sweeps. Error rows compare the *specific* outcome (`ferror` **and** `errno == EBADF`/`ENOSPC`/`EPIPE`), not just \"both failed\".\n\nTwo safeguards worth flagging:\n- **Stale-artifact guard.** `cargo test` does *not* rebuild a `cdylib`, so the tests would have silently run against an old `.so`. The harness now refuses to run if `libdriver.so` is older than `src/lib.rs`, and `./run_tests.sh` rebuilds first.\n- **Anti-vacuity proof.** 6 mutations of `src/lib.rs` (hex case, byte order, sign extension, wrong length, `len=0`, renamed export) each fail 28–42 tests; the unmutated build fails 0. The rows that survive the hex-case mutation are exactly those whose expected output has no letter digit. Table recorded in `CONFIGS.md`.\n\n**Feature combinations:** `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` table and `CMakeLists.txt` exposes no options, so the complete set is one combination (empty). `run_tests.sh` enumerates it from `Cargo.toml` and would loop over the power set if features were added. I additionally re-ran the whole suite against the `release` artifact (`panic = \"abort\"`) — symbol diff empty, 42/42 pass.\n\n`c_src/` is unmodified (only the required `c_src/build/` output dir was created); `src/lib.rs` is byte-identical to the input translation, since no divergence was found."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1052,"cache_read_input_tokens":113322,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1052,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d2ae33c-b2e9-43b3-ba7f-77de9482b3f7","uuid":"6ba556ef-3491-4b7f-86c8-882c6424d6b4","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:45:11.045Z"}
